\\begin{lemma}[Involution and self-duality]\\label{lem:involution}
Let "'$'"\\tau:\\Uq(\\bm)\\to\\Uq(\\bp)"'$ be the anti-algebra isomorphism
$'"\\hK_i\\mapsto\\hK_i"'^{-1}$, $F_r'"\\mapsto E_r"'$.  Then
$'"\\la x,y\\ra=\\la\\tau x,\\tau y\\ra"'$ and the mixed relations for
$c(2,'"\\cdot)"'$ past $b('"\\cdot,\\cdot)"'$ are obtained from those of
$b('"\\cdot,\\cdot)"'$ past $c(2,'"\\cdot)"'$ by this involution.
