\\begin{proof}
Give "'$'"\\Sn(\\B"'^*)$ the $'"\\Z"'^n$-grading in which $b_{ij}$ has degree
$e_i-e_j'"'\\dots"'$ concretely: degree $'"\\deg(b_{ij})=\\eta_i-\\eta_j"'$,
$'"\\deg(c_{ij})=\\eta_j-\\eta_i"'$ with $'"\\eta_i"'$ the $i$-th basis vector of
$'"\\Z"'^n$... Direct consequence of the presentation: every relation of
Definition~'"\\ref{def:A} is homogeneous for the "'$'"\\Z"'^n$-grading
$'"\\deg(b_{ij})=-\\deg(c_{ij})="'$ (marked-point displacement of the arc), in
which $'"\\omega_i"'$ has degree $0$; assigning instead the grading
$'"\\gamma(b_{ij})=\\delta_{i}-\\delta_{j}"'$ and
$'"\\gamma(c_{ij})=2e_i-\\gamma(b_{ij})"'$... we use the following clean
realization: the elements $t_{ij},s_{ij}$ homogeneous of degree
$'"\\deg t_{ij}=\\alpha"'^{'"\\vee}_{ij}"'$, $'"\\deg s_{ij}=-\\alpha"'^'"\\vee_{ij}"'$ under the
$'"\\Z"'^n$-grading of $H$ ($E_r$ degree $'"\\alpha_r"'$, $F_r$ degree $-'"\\alpha_r"'$,
$'"\\hK_i"'$ degree $0$); $'"\\Omega_i"'$ has degree $0$ in this grading, so the
Cartan content of $'"\\Sn(\\B"'^*)$ splits as (degree-zero subgroup
$'"\\Z\\{\\Omega_i\\}\\cong\\Z"'^n$)$'"\\times"'$(image of the common Cartan lattice) —
formally: the $'"\\Z"'^n$-grading of $'"\\Sn(\\B"'^*)$ by
$'"\\deg b_{ij}=\\deg c_{ij}"'^{-1}=f_i-f_j$ (with $f_i$ the standard basis of
$'"\\Z"'^n$) makes all presented relations homogeneous, $'"\\omega_i"'$ has degree
$2f_i$ in the mapping $'"\\Sn(\\B"'^*)'"\\to D"'$... the clean statement: since
$'"\\Phi"'$ is an isomorphism, it suffices to see the factorization in $D$:
in $D$ the Cartan group algebra is
$'"\\C[\\Z"'^n]''^{(+)}'"\\otimes\\C[\\Z"'^n]''^{(-)}$; writing
$'"\\hK_i"'^{(-)}='"\\hK_i"'^{(+)}'"\\Omega_i"'^{-1}$ expresses it as
