"'$'"\\hK"'^{(-)}$ into the diagonal combination)... completing the normal-order
splitting gives $D=D_0'"\\otimes\\C[\\Omega"'^{'"\\pm}]"'$ with $D_0$ generated by
$E_r,F_s,'"\\hK_i"'^{(+)}$: multiplication is an isomorphism by the PBW basis
of $D$ (Remark~'"\\ref{rem:Dstruct}).
\\end{proof}

\\begin{lemma}[diagonal quotient of the double]\\label{lem:diag}
Let "'$J=('"\\hK_i"'^{(+)}-'"\\hK_i"'^{(-)})_{1'"\\le i\\le n}\\subset D"'$.  Then
