holds; the combinatorial reason is "'$'"\\alpha_j(i+1)+\\alpha_i(j)
\\equiv\\delta"'$-cancelling at $|i-j|=1$ and triviality otherwise.

(c): $s_{i+1,i}t_{i,i+1}
='"\\hK_{i+1}"'^{(-)-1}F_iE_i'"\\hK_{i+1}"'^{(+)}$, and by
Proposition~'"\\ref{prop:EF},
\\[
=\\hK_{i+1}"'^{(-)-1}'"\\Bigl(E_iF_i+\\tht\\cK_i"'^{(+)}
  -'"\\tht\\cK_i"'^{(-)-1}'"\\Bigr)\\hK_{i+1}"'^{(+)}.
'"\\]
Three terms:
\\begin{itemize}
\\item "'$'"\\hK_{i+1}"'^{(-)-1}E_iF_i'"\\hK_{i+1}"'^{(+)}$: reordering to
  $(E_i'"\\hK_{i+1}"'^{(+)})('"\\hK_{i+1}"'^{(-)-1}F_i)$ via '"\\eqref{CL}-laws:
  "'$'"\\hK_{i+1}"'^{(-)-1}$ traverses $E_i$ with $q''^{-'"\\alpha_i(i+1)}=q"'^{-1}$;
